=== STATES (honest) ===
  The web source binds NO data hook — its only hook is `useTranslation` (the P1/S10 facade). It is
  pure presentational layout chrome (three always-available help affordances), so it has NO async
  loadable surface: there is no loading / empty / error / stale / offline branch in the web source.
  Manufacturing those states would invent behaviour the source does not have (covenant #2 + #9), so
  this surface reproduces the states that DO exist — the three real web presentations driven by the
  `iconOnly` prop + the responsive `hidden xl:inline` tier:
    iconOnly   (web iconOnly=true)        : icons only, no key-cap, no labels
    keyCapOnly (web iconOnly=false, < xl) : shortcuts shows the "?" key-cap; labels hidden
    full       (web iconOnly=false, xl)   : every label visible
  All three are previewed (#if DEBUG, light + dark) and unit-asserted (showsKeyCap / showsLabel per
  density). Because there is no data hook, there is no P1/S8 data holder to bind and the view does
  ZERO HTTP — the "bind via state holder, no view HTTP" criterion is satisfied vacuously + the
  decoupled actions go through NotificationCenter, never the network.

